{"title":"Career roadmap — Ship Maintenance Engineer","role":"Ship Maintenance Engineer","summary":"A Ship Maintenance Engineer is responsible for maintaining, inspecting, troubleshooting, repairing, and improving a vessel's machinery and engineering systems. The role covers marine engines, propulsion, pumps, boilers, compressors, generators, auxiliary systems, hydraulics, fuel systems, safety systems, and planned maintenance.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Marine Engineering"},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"★★★★★ — Marine Engineering is the most direct undergraduate pathway."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build marine machinery, thermodynamics, ship systems and maintenance fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work onboard or in shipyards as Junior/Assistant Engineer → Maintenance Engineer"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Engineer, Technical Superintendent or Maintenance Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead fleet maintenance, ship reliability, digital maintenance and marine engineering operations"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Mathematics, physics, chemistry, engineering mechanics, thermodynamics basics"},{"text":"Workshop practice, mechanical systems, safety"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, marine engines, electrical systems, materials"},{"text":"Engine-room equipment, pumps, compressors and machinery labs"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Marine propulsion, auxiliary machinery, ship systems, hydraulics, refrigeration, automation"},{"text":"Shipyard/shipboard training, machinery inspection"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Maintenance management, marine safety, reliability, planned maintenance, regulations"},{"text":"Shipyard/shipboard internship + maintenance project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Engineering foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering physics"},{"text":"Engineering chemistry"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Materials science"},{"text":"Electrical fundamentals"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Workshop technology"},{"text":"Technical communication"},{"text":"Occupational safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bearings"},{"text":"Shafts"},{"text":"Gears"},{"text":"Pumps"},{"text":"Valves"},{"text":"Compressors"},{"text":"Motors"},{"text":"Heat exchangers"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Mini-project","text":"Study the operating and maintenance requirements of a marine centrifugal pump."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Marine machinery"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Marine diesel engines"},{"text":"Internal combustion engines"},{"text":"Marine boilers"},{"text":"Steam systems"},{"text":"Pumps"},{"text":"Compressors"},{"text":"Heat exchangers"},{"text":"Fresh-water generators"},{"text":"Refrigeration systems"},{"text":"Steering gear"},{"text":"Fuel systems"},{"text":"Lubrication systems"},{"text":"Cooling-water systems"},{"text":"Hydraulic systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn electrical fundamentals:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Generators"},{"text":"Switchboards"},{"text":"Motors"},{"text":"Batteries"},{"text":"Electrical protection"},{"text":"Basic instrumentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to read:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"P&ID diagrams"},{"text":"Machinery drawings"},{"text":"Hydraulic diagrams"},{"text":"Electrical schematics"},{"text":"Equipment manuals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Ship maint